<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laristan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laristan is a historical region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars province</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>, with its main town at Lar. Arid and hot, it lay on the routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-plateau">Iranian plateau</a> and the Gulf ports. It was ruled by a local dynasty until the Safavid conquest of 1601–02 and later became a province and then a county of Fars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laristan.jpg" alt="Laristan" width="320" height="329" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ali Zifan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fars.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
